{
  "_about": [
    "Everything that differs between Lost Cities versions, in one file.",
    "Every value here was read from the jars themselves or measured on a running",
    "server. None of it comes from documentation.",
    "",
    "'servers' are keyed by loader, not by mod version, because one install serves",
    "several mod versions: 7.4.12 and 7.5.1 share a Forge install, 8.2.2 and 8.4.1",
    "share a NeoForge one. The mod jar is swapped in per run.",
    "",
    "'capabilities' is what a version can actually do. A probe declaring 'requires'",
    "against something absent here reports n/a rather than failing, because a",
    "version that cannot pin a city has not failed a pinning test.",
    "",
    "'registries' is the ONLY thing the rig rewrites inside a pack. A folder the",
    "version did not compile in is never scanned, so the pack silently looks empty.",
    "Nothing else is adapted: an undeclared key is the thing under test.",
    "",
    "To stop the rig printing download links, delete the 'url' fields."
  ],

  "rcon": { "port": 25575, "password": "lcwiki" },

  "javas": {
    "8": {
      "why": "Minecraft 1.12.2. Forge boots through LaunchWrapper, which casts the system class loader to URLClassLoader. Java 9 stopped it being one, and there is no workaround.",
      "url": "https://adoptium.net/temurin/releases/?version=8"
    },
    "17": {
      "why": "Minecraft 1.18.2 through 1.20.1.",
      "url": "https://adoptium.net/temurin/releases/?version=17"
    },
    "21": {
      "why": "Minecraft 1.21 and 1.21.11.",
      "url": "https://adoptium.net/temurin/releases/?version=21"
    },
    "25": {
      "why": "Minecraft 26.1.2. Its class files are version 69, which Java 21 refuses.",
      "url": "https://adoptium.net/temurin/releases/?version=25"
    }
  },

